Checks
Small checks used by the other scripts: that files exist, that required columns or keys are present, and that a step did not change the number of rows. Each stops with a message naming what is missing, never a data value.


Click to show/hide R Code
# Stop if any of the files is missing, naming them.
check_files_exist &lt;- function(paths) {
  missing &lt;- paths[!file.exists(paths)]
  if (length(missing) &gt; 0) {
    stop("Missing file(s): ", paste(missing, collapse = ", "),
         ". See README.md, Running the analysis.", call. = FALSE)
  }
  invisible(TRUE)
}

# Stop if any required name is absent, naming the missing ones and the source.
check_names_present &lt;- function(present, required, source) {
  missing &lt;- setdiff(required, present)
  if (length(missing) &gt; 0) {
    stop(source, " lacks: ", paste(missing, collapse = ", "), call. = FALSE)
  }
  invisible(TRUE)
}

# Stop if a step changed the number of rows.
check_rows_unchanged &lt;- function(before, after, step) {
  if (before != after) {
    stop(step, " changed the number of rows (", before, " to ", after, ").",
         call. = FALSE)
  }
  invisible(TRUE)
}

Record corrections
Applies the corrections listed for one data source: each names a record by its identifier and sets one field to a new value. A correction that matches no record, or more than one, stops the run, so a correction can never be applied silently to the wrong record or skipped. The messages name the source and field, not the identifier.


